 "title": "Microbial Metabolism and Ethanol Production",
 "summary": "This cluster revolves around the microorganisms S. stipitis and P. manshurica, which are involved in ethanol production and have antimicrobial properties. S. stipitis produces various folate vitamers and has upregulated genes XYL1 and XYL2. The pentose phosphate pathway has a high flux in S. stipitis, and glycolysis is a metabolic process in P. manshurica. High-yield strains 31.1 and strain 1960 have faster gas production and higher ethanol yields than low-yield strains. Carvacrol has antimicrobial properties against P. manshurica and induces gas production.",
